WEBVTT

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:07.970
Audrey and Banagher
are reunited aboard the Nahel Argama,

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.930
but the ship is attacked
by the Neo Zeon leader Full Frontal,

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.470
who is said to be
the second coming of the Red Comet.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.510
Frontal demands they give him
the Unicorn Gundam,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.260
the key to LaPlace's Box.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.510
Audrey, whose is revealed
to be the Zeon princess Mineva Zabi

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:27.510
is taken hostage by the desperate crew
of the Nahel Argama.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.470
If we take down that red mobile suit, then
you won't need Audrey as a hostage, right?

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.840
I'll do it!

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.590
In order to save Audrey,

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.550
Banagher once again
gets inside the Unicorn Gundam

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.180
and does battle against Full Frontal,
only to be captured.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.470
I'm sorry, Audrey...

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.880
Banagher is taken to
the Neo Zeon stronghold Palau,

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.590
where the masked Full Frontal is waiting to
meet him in person.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.970
Char Aznable...

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:27.630
What are you doing? Have a seat.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.220
(UNDER THE MASK)

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.260
(UNDER THE MASK)

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.010
How're you feeling?

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.840
I hear we went through a lot
to get you safely out of that Gundam.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.180
Well...

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.800
Were you the pilot
of that red mobile suit?

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.550
You can't drink tea with a mortal enemy,
Banagher Links?

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:06.800
Good reflexes.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.760
But a little reckless.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.550
A temperament befitting a pilot.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.510
If you don't mind me asking...

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:27.760
Do you wear that mask
to hide some kind of scar?

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.680
Because if not,
I'd like you to show me your face.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.630
You- -!

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:37.300
It's fine, Lieutenant Angelo.
Banagher's talking about simple etiquette.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.800
I only wear it because it's my style.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.380
Or you could say
it's a tool of propaganda.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.260
Without someone like you
to point it out to me,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.930
I usually forget I even have it on.

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.220
My apologies.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.760
I've heard about
how you met Princess Mineva.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.930
But as for
how you received that mobile suit,

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.010
that Unicorn Gundam
from the Vist Foundation

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.680
there is much that remains unclear.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.430
We were supposed to receive that machine.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:22.050
So why did Cardeas Vist choose you
to be the bearer of Laplace's Box?

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.680
They asked me that
while I was being escorted here,

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:28.090
and I told them all I know.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.800
The glory of the Vist Foundation was built
on its secret possession of the Box.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.550
But they decided to break the pact
with the Federation government

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.380
and hand it over to us.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:42.800
So their plan couldn't be altered easily.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.340
Even if the original plan had gone awry

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.550
I can't believe he'd entrust the Box
to a random stranger.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.470
It's more likely

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.880
that you have some relation
to the Vist family.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.010
Am I obligated to respond to that?

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.970
I said stop it, Angelo.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.010
You'd better realize
who you're talking to, punk.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.760
You're not obligated to respond.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:16.010
We simply want information about the Box.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.720
We're only asking you nicely

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.470
because you're acquainted
with Princess Mineva.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.630
Keep that in mind.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.050
"Mineva"...

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:29.510
Audrey is the one who told me Neo Zeon
mustn't get their hands on the Box.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.130
She said it would lead to
another great war.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.800
And after what happened

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.470
to our colony, Industrial 7,
anyone would feel the same way.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.840
She is a Princess of Zeon, right?

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.630
If Audrey is against it,
why are all of you- -

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.090
Tell me, do you believe in it?
In the existence of Laplace's Box?

00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.550
Do you believe there's a box
no one has ever seen

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:57.930
and whose contents are unknown

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:02.220
but hides the power to completely destroy
the Federation government?

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:06.180
Well, I really don't know.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:10.180
But I believe
there's such a thing as knowledge

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.930
which can change the world in an instant.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.130
Such as?

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:20.590
For example, like Zeon's first colony drop,

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.090
or dropping an asteroid
to freeze the Earth,

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:25.880
or in the older eras
when nuclear bombs were created,

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:28.930
or when Minovsky particles were discovered,
or mobile suits were invented.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:33.840
Even though it seems stable,
the world changes little by little.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:37.970
If an invention or experiment has that
kind of power, and the timing is right...

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.680
You're right about that.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.760
And if you know your history so well

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:47.340
you know that space settlement was
a policy to exile mass populations, right?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:51.010
You probably realize that even when
a Side's autonomy is recognized

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:55.510
the central government retains
the right to appoint its leaders.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:59.430
Since they can't vote for
the central government,

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.470
the Spacenoids
may as well have no suffrage.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.840
Neo Zeon is not a monolithic society.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:13.010
But we all share the desire
to change this distorted system.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.010
In order to break
the chains of the Federation

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:18.550
and realize Spacenoid autonomy,
we need to- -

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.340
But it's wrong to resort to terrorism!

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:25.180
Whatever your reasons,
you can't arbitrarily take lives!

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.090
No one has that right!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.130
That goes for you too!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.840
If force is always wrong,
you're just as guilty for using the Gundam!

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:43.590
You killed one of our valued men
out there!

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.880
I... what...?

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.930
It may have been a stray shot, but
you're still the one who shot him down!

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.180
I don't think that realization
has hit Banagher yet.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.550
He probably acted out of desperation.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:01.800
Ensign Sergi was unlucky.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:04.720
I... killed someone.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.130
Call for Zinnerman.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.380
You have a lot to learn yet.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.550
I want you to understand who we are.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:18.550
And I hope
we can eventually work together.

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:31.300
Are you...are you really Char Aznable?

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:38.630
As I am now, I consider myself a vessel.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.930
A vessel for the hopes
of those abandoned in space,

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:45.510
and for the heirs of Zeon's ideals.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:52.300
And if that's what they want,
I will be Char Aznable.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.510
That's why I wear this mask.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.130
Palau.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:19.300
It's a civilian mining asteroid
belonging to Side 6.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:25.050
Our intelligence agency has concluded
that the RX-0 was taken here.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:29.840
The Nahel Argama is supposed to break into
that fortress alone? Not possible.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:32.510
This operation is under ECOAS jurisdiction.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.380
Reinforcements have already arrived
for that purpose.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.340
It's unprecedented
for two elite ECOAS teams

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.180
to join forces like this...

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.550
What are our odds?

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.130
If we're supposed to recapture the RX-0,

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.340
seizing control of one area
isn't going to cut it.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:49.300
Amazing! It's Hyaku Shiki!

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:55.220
We'll need to sabotage a wide area
in order to prevent enemy pursuit.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:57.430
Do you agree with this plan, Captain?

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.680
If we're going to attack a stronghold,

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.090
shouldn't we assemble
all of Londo Bell's forces?

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:09.510
It seems like Headquarters is asking us
to go on a suicide mission.

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:14.300
That's why we're sending out
two expensive teams of special forces.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.220
That's the best we can manage
for a covert operation.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.970
We're not asking you!

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:23.050
The RX-0 is lost now
because of what you did!

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.180
Exactly!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.220
The situation developed
in an unexpected way but...

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:30.050
If it hadn't been for that,
the ship would have been destroye- -

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:33.930
I'll be right back.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.090
Damn it!

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.260
You call those reinforcements?!

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.130
You call this a covert operation?!

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:51.050
Spouting desperate excuses
to make up for his own failure!

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:53.180
Damn you!

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.840
We've heard about our orders
from Headquarters.

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.720
What do you intend to do?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:08.340
We have no choice but to go.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:10.050
Because it's related to the Box

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:12.510
which is supposed
to determine the fate of the world.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.970
I have no objection
to our orders either...

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:20.930
But we consider it
a hostage rescue mission.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:26.430
We owe it to him. And I know of a way.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:30.970
This ship is equipped with a
hyper mega particle gun, isn't it?

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.010
The Federation's movement has me concerned.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:42.300
Depending on the situation,
we might need to abandon this place.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.930
You think the Federation
is going to attack?

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:50.430
How's the analysis
of the Unicorn Gundam going?

00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:09.010
Hey, are you from the Federation?

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:11.180
Tikva, be quiet and eat.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.260
These guys forced me to come here.

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.550
Sit still and eat properly, young lady.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.510
You're a prisoner?

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.680
Something like that.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:23.220
Oh, then you're lucky to be our prisoner!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:27.260
If you were a Federation prisoner,
they wouldn't give you anything to eat.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.010
You'd be tortured!

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:31.510
Tikva, don't talk while you're eating.

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.430
The Federation doesn't do things like that.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.880
Yeah, they do. My dad says so.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:40.010
He was a prisoner on Earth,
and the Captain helped him in the camp.

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.680
Well, there are many people

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:45.510
whose friends and family
were killed by Zeon.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:51.430
Yeah, same goes for us obviously.
That's war.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.340
But Zeon was fighting for the Spacenoids.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.380
And you're a Spacenoid, aren't you?

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.720
How come you're on the Federation's side?

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.470
That's enough. You'll make your dad angry.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:04.180
No war is ever justified.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.340
Even if what you're saying is "right"

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:09.130
that doesn't change the fact that

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.050
Zeon dropped an entire colony
and killed lots of people.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.840
The people who were killed

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:18.340
never had a chance
to think about what was "right" or not.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.630
They didn't know anything about it,
and then one day, suddenly...

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.340
It just wasn't fair.

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.220
That's right. Not fair at all.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:28.010
There was nothing else I could do.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.800
I never intended to kill, but...

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:32.180
I was about to be killed.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:36.300
I am not a murderer.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.880
Come with me.

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:58.550
What you're saying is not wrong.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:02.840
There is no truly justifiable war, but...

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.430
...justice does not always save lives.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:19.090
This was built back when Palau
was still in the asteroid belt.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.090
When you think about
the earliest space pioneers

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.970
they were mostly beggars
and political criminals,

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.510
without any other way to live.

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.930
I hear that
when the Universal Century began

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.970
the Prime Minister stated in his speech

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.380
that we were
"bringing an end to the Era of God", but

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.220
the people living in the asteroid belt,

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.840
where the sun
is indistinguishable from any other stars,

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.760
probably needed a light to guide them.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.130
A light...

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.970
No one can live without light.

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:56.380
But the people abandoned in space
eventually found a light to replace God.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:00.630
A new light called Zeon.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.220
It was what they needed.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:10.510
So that they could resist despair
and keep living in this cruel world.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:15.800
Something that made them think there was
room in this world for improvement.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.630
Some might say you can live without that.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.880
Or that it's stupid to cling
to something so intangible.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:25.680
If they're sure about that

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:32.340
those people must be true optimists
or completely detached from reality.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:40.090
Humanity alone possesses a God.

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.180
Someone once told me that.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:49.260
The power to transcend the now,
the inner God called "possibility".

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.880
He must have been a romantic.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:56.430
A person can't say that
without faith in humanity and the world.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.720
Sounds like a nice person.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:03.050
Ensign Sergi...

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:07.050
Don't worry about the one you shot down.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:10.680
When anyone goes into battle
in a mobile suit,

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:13.430
they become a combat unit called a pilot.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.010
There's no need for regrets.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:17.720
But...

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:22.470
Keep in mind that you are already
a part of the situation.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:28.090
And as for taking action
to help Princess Mineva,

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.380
I'm grateful to you.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:34.800
Do you- -

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:35.930
Umm...

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:39.590
Marida.

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:43.300
Do you pilot a mobile suit too,
Ms. Marida?

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.590
When we're short on manpower, yes.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.760
Time to eat.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.880
Better finish before the ship
starts combat operations.

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:05.380
It's you...

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:11.880
Come with me.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.130
We're going to Earth.

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:42.930
Sorry man.

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:46.760
Wait!

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:53.090
What's wrong?

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.470
Nothing...

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:13.550
14th space gate... 3rd port...

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:14.930
By 00:00:00 Zulu...

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:16.590
Stay on schedule...

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:17.930
The safety of your life...

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:20.260
Your life!

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:29.840
This time...

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.630
this place is going to be a battlefield?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:51.850
Message from ECOAS.
"Object ball placed in pyramid spot," sir.

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:56.600
Attention!
Initiate Phase 3.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:00.970
This ship will now breach enemy
airspace at maximum combat speed

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:05.850
and attack the Neo Zeon stronghold
with our hyper mega particle cannon.

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:08.720
This one strike will determine
the success of the mission.

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:11.680
I expect all crew members
to do their utmost.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:53.140
Nashiri Team is proceeding to Phase 2.

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:56.510
Right. Now proceeding
to target retrieval point.

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.430
Once Banagher Links' retrieval
has been confirmed,

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:03.220
we'll join with Team Alpha
to recapture the Gundam.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.970
This will be a hit-and-fade operation.

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:10.560
After the advance team has separated
Palau's four asteroids,

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.680
we'll fire the hyper mega particle
cannon to seal off the military port.

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:18.470
The plan is to retrieve Banagher Links
and the Unicorn while this is going on.

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:22.510
I take it that you will attack only
Palau's military facilities?

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:25.060
Yes. The Federation
has spies there, too.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:31.680
We wouldn't come up with a plan that
would damage the residential block.

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:35.640
That look on your face
says you'll go back

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:37.560
and inform your people
by yourself if you have to.

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:41.560
You'll just have to
take my word for it.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:56.140
We may be at our closest approach,
but it's still two days to Earth.

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:59.640
I could only scrounge up the bare
minimum of food and water.

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.220
I'm prepared to do what I must.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:02.850
What's going on,
Mr. Ensign?

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:08.260
Are you helping the prisoner escape?
Where are you taking that girl?

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.760
Please, just wait. I can't tell you
exactly what's going on, but- -

00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:14.060
Ensign Riddhe!

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:18.100
We're going to Earth.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.640
Just because the Ensign is coming
with me does not mean in any way

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:24.720
that he is betraying the Federation,
or you and your friends.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:31.720
I realized that in these circumstances,
there is something that only I can do.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:32.680
As did Ensign Riddhe.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.310
Like I could believe anything
that the Zeons' princess says!

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.970
It's of vital importance.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:44.850
To prevent this from escalating further,
this is all that I can do right now.

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:53.510
Ms. Micott...

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.260
This doesn't mean I've forgiven you.

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:58.220
You owe me one.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:01.220
Go fulfill your responsibilities
on Earth as best you can.

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:41.560
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn

00:23:41.600 --> 00:23:43.600
THE BATTLE AT PALAU,

00:23:45.140 --> 00:23:48.470
awaken the Newtype that lies within you.
